WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.362
This is how AgentOS goes onto your own Linux
server, from the first call to your first
report.

2
00:00:06.162 --> 00:00:13.546
It starts with an intro call. You tell us
how your agency handles leads and client
reports today, and we agree what to set up
first.

3
00:00:14.346 --> 00:00:21.823
In your setup call, we hand you the Agency
Package. It is one folder, and everything
you need is inside it. Copy it to your
server.

4
00:00:22.623 --> 00:00:31.451
Let us look at what is inside. The install
script, two ready agents, a report theme,
and demo data so you can try everything
before using real leads.

5
00:00:32.251 --> 00:00:40.007
Before installing, check your server. You
need Linux and Python 3.12 or newer. One
command shows your Python version.

6
00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:49.491
The schedules run as systemd user services.
If your server has no systemd, the script
has a manual mode. For PDF reports you also
add playwright.

7
00:00:50.291 --> 00:00:57.861
Run the install script with the dry run
flag. It prints every step it would take,
and writes nothing to your disk. Read the
list first.

8
00:00:58.661 --> 00:01:05.395
When the preview looks right, run the same
command without the dry run flag. The script
then does the work in three parts.

9
00:01:06.195 --> 00:01:17.201
The install makes the folders, a Python
environment and a settings file. It also
sets a daily timer at eight and a weekly
timer on Monday at seven. Each client gets a
separate install.

10
00:01:18.001 --> 00:01:26.314
Now try the first tool on the bundled sample
leads. One command scores five demo leads,
writes them to a table, and creates a short
daily summary.

11
00:01:27.114 --> 00:01:38.863
Lead Triage scores every new lead from zero
to one hundred, using budget, urgency and
fit. It sorts them into hot, warm and cold,
and tells your sales team who to call within
a day.

12
00:01:39.663 --> 00:01:49.791
Leads can come in three ways: a JSON file
you fill in, an email inbox that is only
read, or a webhook when you run the full
AgentOS setup.

13
00:01:50.591 --> 00:02:00.761
Next, Client Reporting. Point it at the CRM
table, pick a week and a client name, and it
writes the report as an HTML file you open
in your browser.

14
00:02:01.561 --> 00:02:14.704
Client Reporting collects one week of
numbers from the CRM: new and qualified
leads, the change from last week, and
estimated revenue from hot leads. The result
is an HTML report, with PDF if you want it.

15
00:02:15.504 --> 00:02:26.400
From now on, the timers do the routine. Lead
Triage runs every morning at eight, and the
weekly report is written every Monday at
seven. You only read the results.

16
00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:32.768
Done. Need help? Email founder at
ironvisiontools dot com.
